      "Name matching against consolidated lists is only the first step. The legal tests extend to entities owned or controlled by designated persons, and ownership may be held indirectly, through trusts, or spread among relatives and associates in ways intended to fall beneath a 50 per cent threshold.",
      "## Looking through the structure",
      "Investigative due diligence examines corporate registers, shareholder records, historic filings and credible media reporting to build an ownership map. Where information is limited, we describe the gaps clearly so that compliance teams can escalate, request more from the counterparty, or decline to proceed.",
      "Control can be as important as ownership. Board appointments, shareholder agreements, powers of attorney and long-standing financial relationships may show that a designated person exerts influence even without a formal majority stake. These facts need careful, balanced interpretation.",
      "We also warn against over-reliance on any single database. Records can be outdated, transliteration of names causes both false positives and false negatives, and some jurisdictions publish little. Combining automated screening with human review produces better outcomes.",
      "Interpreting whether a particular dealing is prohibited, or whether to apply for a licence, is a matter for specialist sanctions solicitors. Our contribution is lawful, documented research that makes their advice better informed."
